### Title and Subtitle

The `title` and `subtitle` are the primary text fields on each card.

```js format="snippet"
{
    series: [
        {
            type: 'organization',
            title: { key: 'name', fontSize: 16, fontWeight: 'bold' },
            subtitle: { key: 'jobTitle', fontSize: 12, color: '#666' },
        },
    ],
}
```

### Labels

Additional information can be displayed using the `label` array. Each entry maps a data field via its
`key` and is stacked vertically below the subtitle.

```js format="snippet"
{
    series: [
        {
            type: 'organization',
            title: { key: 'name' },
            subtitle: { key: 'jobTitle' },
            label: [
                { key: 'department', fontSize: 11, color: '#888' },
                { key: 'location', fontSize: 11, color: '#888' },
            ],
        },
    ],
}
```

Each label supports a `styler` callback for per-node text customisation.

### Image

Cards can include an image, such as a profile photo. The `image` property supports configuring the
shape, size, and position within the card.

```js format="snippet"
{
    series: [
        {
            type: 'organization',
            image: {
                key: 'photoUrl',
                shape: 'circle',
                width: 48,
                height: 48,
                position: 'left',
            },
        },
    ],
}
```

The `position` property controls where the image appears within the card. The `shape` can be
`'circle'` or `'square'`.

## Layout

The chart uses a vertical (top-to-bottom) layout, with the root node at the top and children arranged
below.

{% imageCaption imagePath="resources/layout-top-to-bottom.svg" alt="Organisation chart with vertical (top to bottom) layout" maxWidth="80%" constrained=true centered=true enableDarkModeFilter=true /%}

## Connectors

Connectors are the lines drawn between parent and child nodes. They are configured through the `link`
property and use orthogonal step routing by default.

{% tabs omitFromOverview=true %}

{% tabItem id="connector-elbow" label="Step" %}
{% imageCaption imagePath="resources/connectors-step.svg" alt="Organisation chart with step connectors using right-angle routing" maxWidth="80%" constrained=true centered=true enableDarkModeFilter=true /%}
{% /tabItem %}

{% tabItem id="connector-step-rounded" label="Step (Rounded)" %}
{% imageCaption imagePath="resources/connectors-step-rounded.svg" alt="Organisation chart with step connectors using rounded corners" maxWidth="80%" constrained=true centered=true enableDarkModeFilter=true /%}
{% /tabItem %}

{% /tabs %}

The `cornerRadius` property rounds the corners where the horizontal line drops down toward children.

```js format="snippet"
{
    series: [
        {
            type: 'organization',
            link: {
                interpolation: {
                    type: 'step',
                    cornerRadius: 8,
                },
            },
        },
    ],
}
```

### Connector Styling

Connectors can be styled globally or per-connector using the `link.itemStyler` callback.

```js format="snippet"
{
    series: [
        {
            type: 'organization',
            link: {
                stroke: '#999',
                strokeWidth: 2,
                itemStyler: ({ datum }) => {
                    if (datum.department === 'Engineering') {
                        return { stroke: '#43A047' };
                    }
                },
            },
        },
    ],
}
```

The `itemStyler` callback receives the parent and child data for each connector, allowing
conditional styling based on relationship data.

## Collapse and Expand

Nodes with children can be collapsed and expanded by clicking. Non-leaf nodes display a visual
indicator to show that they can be expanded or collapsed.

{% note %}
The exact visual design of the expand/collapse indicator (badge, pill, or chevron) is still being
finalised. An indicator will be present at launch to distinguish leaf nodes from non-leaf nodes.
{% /note %}

{% tabs omitFromOverview=true %}

{% tabItem id="state-expanded" label="Expanded" %}
{% imageCaption imagePath="resources/state-expanded.svg" alt="Organisation chart with all nodes expanded" maxWidth="80%" constrained=true centered=true enableDarkModeFilter=true /%}
{% /tabItem %}

{% tabItem id="state-collapsed" label="Collapsed" %}
{% imageCaption imagePath="resources/state-collapsed.svg" alt="Organisation chart with collapsed nodes" maxWidth="80%" constrained=true centered=true enableDarkModeFilter=true /%}
{% /tabItem %}

{% /tabs %}

### Initial State

The `initialState.collapsed` property controls which nodes start collapsed when the chart first renders.
By default, all nodes are expanded. Provide a list of node IDs whose subtrees should be hidden.

This uses the same state format as `getState()` and `setState()` described below.

```js format="snippet"
{
    initialState: {
        collapsed: ['finance', 'hr'],
    },
    series: [
        {
            type: 'organization',
        },
    ],
}
```

The `collapsed` set can include leaf node IDs — this has no visible effect, but if children are later
added to that node via a data update, it will already be collapsed.

### Programmatic Control

The chart state can be read and updated programmatically using `getState()` and `setState()`.
The state format is the same as `initialState`. `setState()` performs a full replacement — to toggle
a single node, read the current state, modify the array, then set it back.

```js
// Read the current expand/collapse state
const state = chart.getState();
// state.collapsed = ['finance', 'hr']

// Collapse a specific subtree
chart.setState({ collapsed: ['finance', 'hr', 'marketing'] });
```

### Active Item Auto-Expand

When a node is set as the active item programmatically (via `initialState.active`), all its collapsed
ancestors are automatically expanded and the viewport pans to centre on it. This enables deep-linking
to a specific person in a large chart.

## Tooltips

Tooltips are disabled by default. When enabled, they display all label fields for the hovered node.

```js format="snippet"
{
    series: [
        {
            type: 'organization',
            tooltip: {
                enabled: true,
            },
        },
    ],
}
```

A `tooltip.renderer` callback can be used for custom formatting. The renderer receives the node's
`datum`, `depth`, `childCount`, and all configured label values.

## Event Handling

The `nodeClick` event fires when a node card is clicked, providing the node's data and tree context.

```js format="snippet"
{
    series: [
        {
            type: 'organization',
            listeners: {
                nodeClick: (event) => {
                    console.log('Clicked:', event.datum);
                    console.log('Depth:', event.depth);
                    console.log('Expanded:', event.isExpanded);
                    console.log('Children:', event.childCount);
                },
            },
        },
    ],
}
```

The event payload includes:

-   `datum` — The data object for the clicked node.
-   `depth` — The depth of the node in the tree (root = 0).
-   `isExpanded` — Whether the node is currently expanded.
-   `childCount` — The number of direct children.

## Customisation

### Node Styling

The `itemStyler` callback provides per-node visual customisation based on data and tree state.

```js format="snippet"
{
    series: [
        {
            type: 'organization',
            itemStyler: ({ datum, depth, isExpanded }) => {
                if (depth === 0) {
                    return { fill: '#1565C0', stroke: '#0D47A1' };
                }
                if (datum.department === 'Engineering') {
                    return { fill: '#E8F5E9', stroke: '#43A047' };
                }
            },
        },
    ],
}
```

The callback receives:

-   `datum` — The node's data object.
-   `depth` — The node's depth in the tree.
-   `isExpanded` — Whether the node is expanded.

It can return: `fill`, `stroke`, `strokeWidth`, `opacity`, `cornerRadius`, `lineDash`.

### Label Styling

Each label in the `label` array supports a `styler` callback for per-node text customisation.

```js format="snippet"
{
    series: [
        {
            type: 'organization',
            label: [
                {
                    key: 'department',
                    styler: ({ datum }) => {
                        if (datum.department === 'Engineering') {
                            return { color: '#2E7D32', fontWeight: 'bold' };
                        }
                    },
                },
            ],
        },
    ],
}
```

## Navigation

Large organisation charts often exceed the visible area. Click and drag on the chart background to pan
across the hierarchy.

The viewport automatically centres on the root node when the chart first renders. After expanding or
collapsing a node, the view adjusts to keep the interacted node visible.

## Keyboard Navigation

Organisation Charts support full keyboard navigation. Arrow keys map to the visual layout of the tree:

| Key       | Action                            |
| --------- | --------------------------------- |
| **Up**    | Move to parent                    |
| **Down**  | Move to first child (if expanded) |
| **Left**  | Move to previous sibling          |
| **Right** | Move to next sibling              |
| **Enter** | Toggle expand/collapse            |

Screen readers announce the node content and sibling position (e.g. "3 of 5").

## Should-Have (v2)

The following features are planned for a future release.

### Highlighting

Hovering over a node will highlight the tree path — the node itself, its ancestors, and its descendants.
Nodes and connectors outside the highlighted path will be dimmed.

{% imageCaption imagePath="resources/highlight-tree-path.svg" alt="Tree path highlighting showing ancestors and descendants" maxWidth="80%" constrained=true centered=true enableDarkModeFilter=true /%}

```js format="snippet"
{
    series: [
        {
            type: 'organization',
            highlightStyle: {
                item: {
                    fill: '#E3F2FD',
                    stroke: '#1565C0',
                    strokeWidth: 2,
                },
                unhighlightedBranch: {
                    opacity: 0.3,
                },
            },
        },
    ],
}
```

### Horizontal Layout

A `direction` property will support `'horizontal'` layout (left-to-right), with automatic mirroring
in right-to-left (RTL) locales.

{% imageCaption imagePath="resources/layout-left-to-right.svg" alt="Organisation chart with horizontal (left to right) layout" maxWidth="80%" constrained=true centered=true enableDarkModeFilter=true /%}

### Display Modes

The `displayMode` property will control how much detail each card shows.

{% tabs omitFromOverview=true %}

{% tabItem id="display-full" label="Full" %}
{% imageCaption imagePath="resources/display-mode-full.svg" alt="Organisation chart in full display mode showing all card content" maxWidth="80%" constrained=true centered=true enableDarkModeFilter=true /%}
{% /tabItem %}

{% tabItem id="display-compact" label="Compact" %}
{% imageCaption imagePath="resources/display-mode-compact.svg" alt="Organisation chart in compact display mode showing title and subtitle only" maxWidth="80%" constrained=true centered=true enableDarkModeFilter=true /%}
{% /tabItem %}

{% /tabs %}

-   `'full'` — Shows all content: title, subtitle, labels, and image.
-   `'compact'` — Shows only the title and subtitle. Labels and images are hidden.
-   `'auto'` (default) — Automatically switches between full and compact based on available space.

### Smooth and Linear Connectors

Additional connector interpolation types beyond the default `'step'` routing.

{% tabs omitFromOverview=true %}

{% tabItem id="connector-smooth" label="Smooth" %}
{% imageCaption imagePath="resources/connectors-smooth.svg" alt="Organisation chart with smooth Bezier curve connectors" maxWidth="80%" constrained=true centered=true enableDarkModeFilter=true /%}
{% /tabItem %}

{% tabItem id="connector-linear" label="Linear" %}
{% imageCaption imagePath="resources/connectors-linear.svg" alt="Organisation chart with straight diagonal connectors" maxWidth="80%" constrained=true centered=true enableDarkModeFilter=true /%}
{% /tabItem %}

{% /tabs %}

-   `'smooth'` — Bezier curve connectors. The `tension` property (0–1) controls the curve tightness.
-   `'linear'` — Straight diagonal lines between nodes.

### Per-Level Styling

A `depths` array will allow styling overrides per hierarchy level, enabling colour-coded depth tiers
for both cards and labels.

### Zoom

Mouse wheel zoom will be supported as a chart-level navigation capability.

## Could-Have (v3)

The following features are under consideration for future releases.

-   **Drag-to-reorganise** — Rearrange the hierarchy by dragging nodes to new parents.
-   **Secondary relationships** — Dotted-line connectors for multi-reporting structures.
-   **Multi-parent nodes** — Nodes with more than one parent (e.g. family trees, shared resources).
-   **Minimap** — An overview panel for navigating large charts.
-   **Inline editing** — Edit node content directly within the chart.

## API Reference

```js
interface AgOrganizationSeriesOptions {
    type: 'organization';

    /** Array of node records. Each record represents one node in the hierarchy. */
    data?: object[];
    /** Key in data for the unique node identifier. Default: `'id'`. */
    idKey?: string;
    /** Key in data for the parent node identifier. Default: `'parentId'`. */
    parentIdKey?: string;

    /** Primary text field, always visible. */
    title?: {
        key: string;
        fontSize?: number;
        fontWeight?: CSSFontWeight;
        fontFamily?: string;
        color?: string;
        styler?: (params: OrganizationLabelStylerParams) => OrganizationLabelStyle;
    };
    /** Secondary text field, always visible. */
    subtitle?: {
        key: string;
        fontSize?: number;
        fontWeight?: CSSFontWeight;
        fontFamily?: string;
        color?: string;
        styler?: (params: OrganizationLabelStylerParams) => OrganizationLabelStyle;
    };
    /** Additional text fields. */
    label?: Array<{
        key: string;
        fontSize?: number;
        fontWeight?: CSSFontWeight;
        fontFamily?: string;
        color?: string;
        styler?: (params: OrganizationLabelStylerParams) => OrganizationLabelStyle;
    }>;
    /** Image displayed within each card. */
    image?: {
        /** Key in node data for the image URL. */
        key: string;
        /** Shape of the image mask. Default: `'square'`. */
        shape?: 'circle' | 'square';
        /** Width of the image in pixels. */
        width?: number;
        /** Height of the image in pixels. */
        height?: number;
        /** How the image fills its container. Default: `'cover'`. */
        fit?: 'cover' | 'contain' | 'fill';
        /** Position of the image within the card. Default: `'left'`. */
        position?: 'top' | 'left' | 'bottom' | 'right';
    };

    /** Minimum width of each node card (pixels). */
    minWidth?: number;
    /** Maximum width of each node card (pixels). */
    maxWidth?: number;
    /** Fixed height of each node card (pixels). */
    height?: number;
    /** Maximum height of each node card (pixels). */
    maxHeight?: number;
    /** Minimum spacing between nodes (pixels). */
    minSpacing?: number;

    /** Connector line configuration. */
    link?: {
        interpolation?: {
            /** Connector shape. Default: `'step'`. */
            type?: 'step';
            /** Corner rounding (pixels). */
            cornerRadius?: number;
        };
        stroke?: string;
        strokeWidth?: number;
        lineDash?: number[];
        /** Per-connector styling callback. */
        itemStyler?: (params: OrganizationLinkStylerParams) => OrganizationLinkStyle;
    };

    /** Initial expand/collapse state. Same format as getState()/setState(). */
    initialState?: {
        /** Node IDs to collapse. Their subtrees are hidden. All other nodes are expanded by default. */
        collapsed?: Array<string | number>;
    };

    tooltip?: {
        /** Whether to show tooltips on node hover. Default: `false`. */
        enabled?: boolean;
    };

    /** Per-node card styling callback. */
    itemStyler?: (params: OrganizationItemStylerParams) => OrganizationItemStyle;

    listeners?: {
        /** Fired when a node card is clicked. */
        nodeClick?: (event: OrganizationNodeClickEvent) => void;
    };
}
```
